  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A&nbsp;ray of light passes four transparent glass slabs having&nbsp;refractive indices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. If the emergent ray <math> <mrow> <mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow> </math> is&nbsp;parallel to the incident ray <math> <mrow> <mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></math>,&nbsp;then&nbsp;</p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/628295_que_CA.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 147px;\" /></p>\r",
    "image": null
